{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795692567,"nonce":"0171RJbhG+Bz/Jmr72STcVOqKJY=","title":"Desktop audio controls do not follow playback","message":"On desktop, the controls of audio_player() stay as they were when built: the play icon, 0:00, an empty seek bar and the volume. The waveform above them advances. The audio-player preview on the website shows it.\n\nMediaControls::new read its player once. The web build of audio_player and the video widget bind to player signals, so only the desktop audio path and direct users of MediaControls were affected.\n\nTwo things show once the controls follow the player: AudioPlayer::position_ms ran past the end of a finished track, and resume() on a finished track did nothing.\n\nThe recorder also paced only the video demo by the wall clock, so the audio preview covered under a second of playback.\n\nFix: the controls bind to signals of their own and copy the player into them in the paint of a canvas, which asks for frames while the player plays. This works for any Player.\n\nNot covered: the desktop controls (MediaControls: a volume percentage) still differ from the web ones (a mute button and a volume bar), although the web page says both are the same.","files":null}]}